<section class="work-directions page-shell" aria-labelledby="directions-heading">
  <div class="section-heading section-heading--stacked">
    <p class="eyebrow">Disciplines and problems</p>
    <h2 id="directions-heading">The questions are broader than any one product.</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">Five disciplines connect the organization's research questions with practical software and learning.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="discipline-list">
    <article class="discipline-item">
      <span class="discipline-number">01</span>
      <div><h3>Intelligent systems</h3><p>How can model-assisted work use relevant context and tools while keeping its steps and outcomes understandable to a person?</p><p class="discipline-evidence"><strong>Current direction:</strong> ForgeWire, a private application and runtime project described at overview level in its <a href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs/ForgeWire-Overview">public overview</a>.</p></div>
    </article>
    <article class="discipline-item">
      <span class="discipline-number">02</span>
      <div><h3>Distributed computing and execution infrastructure</h3><p>What boundaries matter when work is placed across machines with different capabilities, connectivity, and authorization?</p><p class="discipline-evidence"><strong>Current direction:</strong> Fabric is a private control-plane project exploring authenticated, policy-gated execution. Its overview describes a configuration-dependent connection for selected ForgeWire workflows.</p></div>
    </article>
    <article class="discipline-item">
      <span class="discipline-number">03</span>
      <div><h3>Developer and repository infrastructure</h3><p>How can project intent, authority, work state, decisions, and evidence remain inspectable inside the repository across tools and sessions?</p><p class="discipline-evidence"><strong>Public example:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs/repopact-core">RepoPact Core</a> is a released CLI package with a canonical Rust semantic engine. Workbench is a separate source-build preview.</p></div>
    </article>
    <article class="discipline-item">
      <span class="discipline-number">04</span>
      <div><h3>Systems integration and local software</h3><p>How should independent applications retain clear ownership of their data, responsibilities, and release boundaries as they connect to other tools?</p><p class="discipline-evidence"><strong>Examples:</strong> Anvil is a changing developer preview for planning records; Flink is a separate communication and coordination project with published installer materials still under its former name.</p></div>
    </article>
    <article class="discipline-item">
      <span class="discipline-number">05</span>
      <div><h3>Applied technical education</h3><p>How can structured instruction connect concepts, practice, and feedback in software a learner can use on a local device?</p><p class="discipline-evidence"><strong>Public example:</strong> SkillForge Academy has a published Windows application. Newer course-platform work has its own beta status and is not represented by that release.</p></div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="work-principles" aria-labelledby="principles-heading">
  <div class="page-shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">Working principles</p>
    <h2 id="principles-heading">Make the boundary visible.</h2>
    <div class="principle-grid">
      <article><span>01</span><h3>State who has authority</h3><p>When a tool can change work, its scope and the operator's role should be clear in that project's design.</p></article>
      <article><span>02</span><h3>Keep claims tied to evidence</h3><p>Source, version, environment, tests, and release status matter when describing what software does.</p></article>
      <article><span>03</span><h3>Design for the conditions at hand</h3><p>Compute, provider, connectivity, platform, and recovery constraints are engineering questions, not decorative themes.</p></article>
    </div>
    <p class="principle-note">These principles shape how ForgeWire Labs approaches scope, authority, evidence, and operating constraints.</p>
    <a class="button button-light" href="{{ site.basePath }}/engineering/">Read Research &amp; Engineering <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
  </div>
</section>
